The starter UI lays itself out for narrow and short main windows

The starter UI's dock sits on the right at a fixed width with one bar to a row, made for a desktop window: on a phone
held upright it leaves the main console a sliver, and on one on its side the bars run off its foot.

- It reads its main window's shape from getMainWindowInfo()'s size classes (BaseUI.screenShape()). In a narrow one its
  dock runs along the bottom at full width, 45% high, with the map beside the chat window and the bars two to a row
  under them; in a short one it stays on the right with the bars two to a row. A roomy one, every desktop window of
  the usual size, is laid out as before.
- It follows the shape on sysMainWindowClassChangeEvent and on resizes, and leaves a dock the player moved or sized
  alone.
- It declares setAdaptiveLayout("mudlet-base-ui", true) while it is shown, and false when hidden, stood aside or
  uninstalled. A Mudlet without getMainWindowInfo() gets the roomy layout.
- Version 1.9.7, the mpackage rebuilt.

Tested by UI_spec.lua (the shapes, the bottom dock with the map and chat window side by side, back to the right, a
moved dock left alone, two bars to a row, and the declaration while shown).

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

